WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.884
BioAgent acquires and reuses robot skills for long-horizon biological experiments.

2
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:11.814
Liquid handling and instrument access on a dual-arm robot.

3
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:21.091
The Analyzer extracts human-reviewed requirements. The Planner matches them against
validated skills and identifies missing capabilities.

4
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:31.618
Written instructions become concrete operations, object bindings, and expected outcomes,
reviewed before planning.

5
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:37.475
When a capability is missing, BioAgent requests targeted human demonstrations.

6
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:42.859
The Monitor checks outcomes and governs retries, recovery, or termination.

7
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:53.275
Task one performs plate pretreatment and incubator loading. The complete recording is shown
continuously, without omitted operations.

8
00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.565
Attach a pipette tip.

9
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.433
The robot picks up the reagent tube.

10
00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.125
The reagent tube is uncapped.

11
00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.241
Aspirate reagent from the tube.

12
00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.881
Dispense reagent into the six-well plate.

13
00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.081
The reagent tube is recapped.

14
00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.028
Eject the used pipette tip.

15
00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.615
Return the pipette to its storage position.

16
00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.499
Replace the lid on the six-well plate.

17
00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.755
Open the temperature-controlled incubator.

18
00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.937
Place the six-well plate inside the incubator.

19
00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.985
Close the incubator doors.

20
00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:24.792
A missing aspiration skill triggers a targeted request for human teaching.

21
00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:31.939
The human demonstrates aspiration from the reagent tube during teleoperation.

22
00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:39.655
Accepted observations and actions support an offline policy update, followed by execution
validation.

23
00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:43.761
The robot then performs reagent aspiration independently.

24
00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:49.987
Task two washes the plate. The complete supplied recording is accelerated three times.

25
00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:56.381
Remove the existing liquid from the six-well plate.

26
00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.711
Add cleaning liquid to the six-well plate.

27
00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:17.029
Recap the reagent tube, then mix the plate.

28
00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:22.642
Remove the wash liquid.

29
00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.221
Finish the final labware handling.

30
00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:40.789
Across twenty-five atomic skills, success ranges from eighty-four to one hundred percent.
Seventeen skills succeed in all fifty trials.

31
00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:52.226
Autonomous recovery increases complete-task success from fifty-four to sixty-six percent for
task one, and from forty to fifty-eight percent for task two.

32
00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:58.638
Learn missing skills. Verify execution. Reuse capabilities.
